projects.description:
Support continuation of Eduten gamified learning platform for grade 5th Math lessons after the piloting with Global Learning Innovation Hub;   				
Support conducting country analysis to formulate concrete challenges and possible digital learning futures within Learning pioneering initiative; 				
Organize a series of workshops and discussions to support designing EdTech solutions and how it could be tested and scaled  in Uzbekistan; 				
Support piloting of selected EdTech solutions in the country;

Upgrading of existing infrastructure of 50 model schools against developed accessibility check lists for school accessibility (e.g. entry, ramps, signage, doors, stairs, toilets, furniture, etc.);				
Establishment of digital labs with assistive technologies in model schools;				
Capacity building and training programmes for school management teams, teachers and multidisciplinary inclusion teams in schools				
Introduction of school inclusive Disaster Risk Management plans;

Support to CED in development of competency-based, inclusive and gender transformative requirements to educational standards;				
Support MOPSE in finalizing CBE National Curriculum Framework;			
Support MOPSE/CED in development of roadmap for implementation of NCF;

Support in development of framework and mechanisms for Inclusive Preschools;	
Pilot of frameworks and mechanisms in 10 preschools;			
Design of the Behavior Change Strategy and roll out of the campaign;

Support review and gaps analysis of current knowlwdge and practicies of preschool teachers' and managers and development of recommendations and road map for improving in-service training programme;			
Revision of in-service training programme for teachers based on new curriculum and programme for training managers (along with capacity building of MOPSE Working Group /national experts);				
Equipping Regional Cluster Centres for in-service training (Decentralized) by distribution of equipment, training package for preschool teachers on preschool curriculum & ELDS and managers on preschool management;		
Development of the training programme and materials for the training of Master Trainers and Teachers of In-Service teachers training Institute on new Curricula and Training of Master Trainers;

Strengthen the Government's capacity to understand the importance of child poverty and its implications for child wellbeing, the country’s development and achieving SDGs;
Equip the Government with methods and tools to systematically measure and monitor monetary child poverty;
Equip the Government with methods and tools to systematically measure multidimensional child poverty in line with the international standards to inform policymaking, programs and budgets.

Strengthen the capacity of the Statistics Agency, CERR and MoEPR in the analysis and reporting of the monetary and multidimensional child poverty data and for tracking the progress of implementation of SDGs on poverty.

Developing Learning assessment framework and associated legislation;  				
Methodological support and capacity building for introduction of classroom assessment; 				
Methodological support and capacity building for introduction of classroom assessment  national examination;

Support to MOPSE in revising four subject-specific curricula;				
Support to CED in development of the framework of standards for developing digital and printed TLMs;			
Support to CED in development of a strategy for gender transformative and inclusive TLMs development;

"Support in enhancing of ELDS through validation to age and content;					
Support in capacity-building module on revised preschool curriculum to be integrated into CPL programs;		
Support in development of Teacher and parent guidebooks and play-based TLMs  based on revised ELDS;

Support MOPSE to develop school self-evaluation / quality assurance (framework, mechanisms, standards, tools);
Support MOPSE to develop teacher- and school-leader appraisal (framework, mechanisms, tools) consistent with professional standards and school-evaluation;
Support MOPSE to enhance the system of preschool evaluation and self-evaluation;

Co-creation and validation workshops with government and development partners, teachers, parents and children to develop vision for inclusive education, including road map and IE Guidelines;		
Revision of the Resolution #638 on SoPs for inclusive schools;			
Development of school-based check-lists for assistive technology and equipment and school accessibility;

Reviewing, developing, sharing data on education financing and impact at systems level for transparency and accountability; 				
Identify new mechanisms for budget and sector planning for improved adequacy, efficiency and equity in education financing;				
Strengthening the capacity of the MoPSE on budgeting, planning and engaging with the national budgeting process;

Support review and assesment of existing teacher training curricula, pedagogy to identify gaps;			
Support in revising the pre-service training curriculum and programmes;				
Development of the training programme and materials for the training of Master Trainers and Teachers of Pre-Service teachers training Institute on new Curricula and Capacity building of key personnel;
Support Agency for preschool education under MPSE in finalization of teacher standards and its operationalization;

Regional project focusing on:
-  Capacities to collect, analyze and report data for decision-making on sustainable production, climate change and environmental degradation;
- Mechanisms to identify, monitor threats, and assess risks and deliver integrated and timely Early Warning; 
- Capacities on prevention and mitigation good practices to reduce impacts of threats and crises).

Mainstreaming Gender in teachers' initial education and training through developing a course on Gender and Education  for Teacher Education Institutions;
Strengthened the capacity of teacher education institutions in delivering gender education course
Number of teachers trained on inclusive, gender-sensitive, and innovative pedagogies through remote and blended learning;

MICS secondary data analysis of Education sector as part of MICS Eagle HQ support;				
Development of infographic and factsheet on equity focus in education including dissemination of data linked to result based education financing;				
Integrate data and analytics into education section programming and coordination;

"- Development of inclusive education conceptual framework, standards/requirements and mechanisms for inclusive and protective preschools and schools;
- Modelling of inclusive pre-schools and schools through the piltoing and operationalization of the standards/requirements and mechanisms developed as part of the conceptual framework and policy for inclusive education;
- Designing of C4D campaign for promoting Inclusive Education, and for eliminating stigma and discrimination, including abuse and violence, against children with disabilities;
- Undertake pre-service and in-service teachers' training to align with new competency-based curriculum and introduce new courses on teaching SEN children
- Exchange of best practices in development and implementation of policies and preschool and school-based practices on Inclusive Education;"
